          "narration": "Now let's see what happens when we have lone pairs\u2014electron pairs not involved in bonding. Lone pairs occupy more angular space than bonding pairs because they are only attracted to one nucleus. This causes the remaining bonding pairs to be compressed together, decreasing bond angles."
